  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, which builds a walking spider from primitives in the existing #app canvas. Typecheck passes, but I couldn't run the app or `vite build`, so I haven't seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Spider:** the body is a cephalothorax sphere and an abdomen sphere, plus abdomen spots, eyes and fangs. Eight legs are attached at the body, four per side. Each leg is a chain of groups (hip, swing, lift, femur, knee, tibia) with a foot sphere, so every leg has two segments and a knee.\n- **Gait:** one gait cycle takes 2 seconds, and time wraps with a modulo, so the loop is seamless. Legs on opposite diagonals move together, and the two diagonals are half a cycle apart. In its half of the cycle, a leg lifts with extra knee extension and swings forward with an eased curve. In the other half it plants and sweeps back.\n- **Bob:** the body bobs up and down twice per cycle, once per step, and rolls slightly from side to side.\n- **Scene:** the `product-studio` look preset supplies the studio backdrop, soft light and shadows. I added a light-grey floor plane that receives shadows. The camera is a three-quarter perspective placed to frame the whole spider.\n- **Contract:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`. Nothing is loaded from outside, and it makes no network requests.\n\nTwo things to check when you run it. The preset's own shadow light may not reach the floor, because I didn't add a separate shadow-casting light. The camera framing is also a calculated guess.\n\n",
